  "notes": "Boot an NBA Fastbreak ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape, step past the power-up TEST REPORT and the game identification, navigate the WPC-95 service menu to T.1 SWITCH EDGES and start it, then drive each public edge separately, holding each level for 2 s: 12 (nbaf.c's swBackboxBasket, the control), then 1, 2, 3 and 4 (WPC_COMPORTS' coin-door column), then 12 again. The ROM's top display line names a switch while it reads it as active, so the name it prints after each address is set to 1 is the ROM's own label for that matrix position.",
